<title>USA: EA Industries names Cannestra chairman.</title>
<headline>EA Industries names Cannestra chairman.</headline>
<dateline>WEST LONG BRANCH, N.J. 1997-07-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>EA Industries Inc said Friday it had named Kenneth Cannestra as chairman of the company's board of directors.</p>
<p>EA said in a statement Cannestra was an executive with Lockheed Martin Corp, where he served as president of aeronautical systems before his retirement in 1995.</p>
<p>Cannestra is replacing Irwin Gross, who has left the company to pursue other interests, a spokeswoman for EA said.</p>
<p>EA is a diversified contract maunufacturer serving the electronics industry through its wholly-owned subsidiary Tanon Manufacturing Inc.</p>
